Gates: SDD

Purpose:
  Universal gate engine for the SDDRA system. Defines gate criteria,
  failure routing, and validation rules for all stages.
  Stage gates are in stage/gates.sdd; security gates are in security/.

Owns: ./

  GateTypes:
  stage: @stage/gates.sdd — stage-specific pass/fail criteria
  security: @security/INDEX.sdd — security gate specifications
  security_enforce: @security-enforcement.sdd — enforcement runtime for security gates
  policy: @policy.sdd — gate policy and waiver rules
  levels: @levels.sdd — adaptive gate levels L0-L5
  quality: @quality.sdd — quality gate criteria
  testing: @testing.sdd — testing gate criteria
  performance: @performance.sdd — performance gate criteria
  infrastructure: @infrastructure.sdd — infrastructure gate criteria
  release: @release.sdd — release gate criteria

Modes:
  L0 — Prototype (minimal checks)
  L1 — Small project (basic test + lint)
  L2 — Production application (security + integration + deployment)
  L3 — Business-critical (performance + security + observability)
  L4 — High-scale (resilience + DR + advanced security)
  L5 — Mission-critical (formal controls + continuous verification)

GateFailure:
  Gate failure MUST route to FailureRouting. The chain MUST NOT advance
  past an ungated stage.

  Routing table:
    code issue      -> responsible implementation stage
    architecture    -> AR
    database        -> DB
    security        -> SC (finding) + responsible stage (fix)
    test gap        -> QA
    infrastructure  -> DO
    requirement     -> HUMAN

GateCriteria:
  Every gate criterion MUST be:
    - Measurable (pass/fail, not subjective)
    - Automated where possible
    - Documented with its evidence source
    - Traceable to a requirement or risk

Rules:
  [GT1]  Task completion ? Release readiness.
  [GT2]  Gates are adaptive: project context determines required gates.
  [GT3]  Every gate MUST have Condition + Evidence + Threshold + Owner + Decision.
  [GT4]  Gate failure blocks subsequent gates in chain.
  [GT5]  SKIPPED ? WAIVED: SKIPPED = not applicable, WAIVED = approved exception.
  [GT6]  Critical gates are hard blockers.
  [GT7]  Evidence MUST be stored for every gate result.
  [GT8]  Gate audit MUST record Who, What, When, Why, Result, Evidence.
  [GT9]  Waivers MUST have Reason, Owner, Expiration, Risk, Approval.
  [GT10] Expired waivers MUST re-trigger gate.
  [GT11] Incident feedback MUST trigger new gate requirements.
  [GT12] Gate chain: BDD ? Code ? Static Quality ? Unit ? Integration ? E2E ? Security ? Performance ? Infrastructure ? Review ? Release ? Deploy ? Runtime Verify.
  [G1]   Every stage MUST have a gate defined in stage/gates.sdd.
  [G2]   A gate MUST declare at least one pass criterion and one fail criterion.
  [G3]   ALL pass criteria MUST be satisfied before the stage is considered complete.
  [G4]   ANY fail criterion MUST block advancement and route to FailureRouting.
  [G5]   Gate criteria MUST be measurable — subjective criteria MUST NOT be used as pass/fail gates.
  [G6]   Gate criteria MAY be automated (test, lint, scan) or manual (review, architecture check), but manual gates MUST be explicitly marked as such.
  [G7]   A stage MUST NOT be marked complete without its gate passing.
  [G8]   Gate failure MUST route to the responsible owner, not to the next stage.
  [G9]   Security Gate (SC) failure at CRITICAL or HIGH MUST block VR regardless of other gate results.
  [G10]  VR Gate failure MUST trigger impact analysis before any backward transition.
  [G11]  A gate MAY be waived only by human decision. AI MUST NOT waive a gate.
  [G12]  Gate criteria are defined at the system level — project-specific additions belong in project/flows.sdd.

ReadOrder:
    1  @policy.sdd
    2  @levels.sdd
    3  @quality.sdd
    4  @testing.sdd
     5  @security/INDEX.sdd
     6  @security-enforcement.sdd
     7  @performance.sdd
    7  @infrastructure.sdd
    8  @release.sdd
    9  @stage/gates.sdd

Navigation:
  Gates: @gates/INDEX.sdd
  Policy: @policy.sdd
  Levels: @levels.sdd
  Quality: @quality.sdd
  Testing: @testing.sdd
  Security: @security/INDEX.sdd
  SecurityEnforcement: @security-enforcement.sdd
  Performance: @performance.sdd
  Infrastructure: @infrastructure.sdd
  Release: @release.sdd
  StageGates: @stage/gates.sdd
  ProjectGates: @projects/{project_name}/gates/INDEX.sdd

State: +
